# ============================================================
# 🧠 CONCEPT: Keeping secrets out of version control
# WHY IT MATTERS (interview angle): "How do you manage secrets?" is a
#   standard question. The answer starts with: .env is NEVER committed;
#   only .env.example (keys, no values) is.
# HOW IT WORKS HERE: git ignores every .env variant, node_modules,
#   build output and uploaded files.
# ============================================================

node_modules/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

server/uploads/*
!server/uploads/.gitkeep

.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
